  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed two-storey upward extension would result in a building of excessive height and massing that fails to respect the established form and character of the industrial estate. The development would appear visually incongruous and dominant within its setting contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG, December 2024)Policy D4 of the London Plan (March, 2021)Policy DMD1 of the LBBD Local Plan (September 2024)",
    "The proposed development fails to demonstrate&nbsp;that additional demand for parking from the development could be adequately accommodated in the surrounding area. The proposal is therefore likely to add unacceptably to parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site.&nbsp; As such, it fails to comply with the following policies&nbsp;which seek to ensure proposals show how car parking will be designed and managed:National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG, December 2024) Policies T1 and T6&nbsp; of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies DMT1 and&nbsp;DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
